      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think the 2 param overload is actually called, but it depends on Camera.main anyway.\n\nFeedback - Add LineRenderer.BakeMesh API which does not require a camera - Unity Forum\n\nhttps://forum.unity.com/threads/add-linerenderer-bakemesh-api-which-does-not-require-a-camera.733679/\n\nClientSim should provide a camera with MainCamera tag on PlayMode, it is not exposed in Udon so there should be no side effects anyway.(PlayerCamera of [1] Local Player should be appropriate. )",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-17T01:20:42.212Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "[UdonSharp] Assets/Ender 3/Scripts/Ender3.cs(561,56): Udon runtime exception detected!\n  An exception occurred during EXTERN to 'UnityEngineTrailRenderer.__BakeMesh__UnityEngineMesh_SystemBoolean__SystemVoid'.\n      Parameter Addresses: 0x00000012, 0x00000038, 0x00000064\n  \n  Value cannot be null.\n  Parameter name: camera\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nthe line in code throwing the error is \n            _trailRenderer.BakeMesh(_trailGeneratedMesh, false);\nDigging deeper it appears to be calling the wrong extern. There is an overload method that takes a camera as the second variable which i believe is being improperly called to. https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/TrailRenderer.BakeMesh.html\nThe extern used\nEXTERN, \"UnityEngineTrailRenderer.__BakeMesh__UnityEngineMesh_SystemBoolean__SystemVoid\"\nFails on 3.0.9 to before 3.0.3",
